<title>RUSSIA: Russian March nickel, aluminium output up mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Russian March nickel, aluminium output up mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian March nickel production rose nine percent from February, and aluminium output increased 11 percent month-on-month over the same period, State Statistics Committee figures showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The committee gave no absolute production figures, but provided the following data --</p>
<p>RUSSIAN NON-FERROUS, PRECIOUS AND MINOR METALS OUTPUT</p>
<p>(all figures expressed as percentage changes)</p>
<p>			    March 1997	   Q1 1997</p>
<p>			    pct change	  pct change</p>
<p>				mth/mth	     yr/yr</p>
<p> Alumina			+5.0		-4.0</p>
<p> Primary aluminium	 +11.0		+1.0</p>
<p> Bauxite			+3.0	     -21.0</p>
<p> Copper concentrate	+16.0	     -14.0</p>
<p> Refined copper	    +12.0		-7.0</p>
<p> Nickel			 +9.0		-2.0</p>
<p> Cobalt			+21.0		+2.0</p>
<p> Zinc			  +21.0		+0.7</p>
<p> Gold			  +14.0	     +32.0</p>
<p> Magnesium (and alloys)   +5.0		-0.3</p>
<p> Titanium sponge	   +12.0	     +58.0</p>
<p> Rolled aluminium	   +7.0	     -21.0</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
